{
  "info": {
    "name": "Week 3 - Full Stack To-Do API (assignment 1)",
    "description": "SkillNexis Week 3, assignment 1. The React client at http://localhost:5173 calls exactly these routes; this collection is the same API without the browser.\n\nRun 'Register user A' first: it saves the JWT into {{token}}, and every /api/tasks request sends it. 'Create a task' saves the new id into {{taskId}}.\n\nThe folder 'Second user - proof tasks are private' registers a different account and tries to read and change user A's task. Every one of those comes back 404: a task can only be reached by the account that owns it, and a 403 would confirm it exists.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
